      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-143384",
      ":question/problem": "The joint probability density function for the continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$f(x, y) = {\\frac{2}{3}xy^{3},\\begin{vmatrix}2 \\le x \\le 4, 0 \\le y \\le 1, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$.\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $f_{X}(x) = 2x$ for $x \u2208 [2, 4]$\n2. $f(x, y) = f_{X}(x) \\cdot f_{Y}(y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$\n3. $X$ and $Y$ are independent"
